In article <1993Apr3.145949.10844@mnemosyne.cs.du.edu> jcopelan@nyx.cs.du.edu (The One and Only) writes:
>Do silver sabers get special damage against demons (or any undead, for
>that matter)?  Is it enough to favor them over artifacts when fighting
>these types of monsters?

Spoilers...

Silver does extra damage against several critters, including demons.
It does an extra 1 to 20 points.  You'll get a message about silver
searing the monster.

One artifact is a silver saber, called Grayswandir.  This does double
damage against anything it hits.  A blessed +7 Grayswandir wielded by
a character with 18/** strength can do 83 points of damage in a single
blow!  The average damage is 39 points against silver-hating monsters.
It is particularly nice against ice devils, who don't care much about
Frost Brand.  Near the end of the game, the Wizard tends to call up a
lot of devils and demons.  For the end of the game, Grayswandir is
clearly the most effective artifact.  Frost Brand is slightly more
effective (avg 4 points) against large, non-cold-resistant monsters.

Happy hacking!

